  "question": {
    "text": "If the straight lines $x+3 y=4,3 x+y=4$ and $x+y$ $=0$ form a triangle, then the triangle is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pbqus",
      "text": "\nscalene\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cAV1x",
      "text": "\nequilateral triangle\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Bjy6c",
      "text": "\nisosceles\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ub54Z",
      "text": "\nright angled isosceles",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let equation of $A B: x+3 y=4$\nLet equation of $B C: 3 x+y=4$\nLet equation of $C A: x+y=0$\nNow, By solving these equations we get $A=(-2,2), B=(1,1)$ and $C=(2,-2)$\nNow, $A B=\\sqrt{9+1}=\\sqrt{10}$,\n$$\nB C=\\sqrt{1+9}=\\sqrt{10}\n$$\nand $C A=\\sqrt{16+16}=\\sqrt{32}$\nSince, length of $A B$ and $B C$ are same\ntherefore triangle is isosceles.",
    "image": null
  },
